Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Sat May 24 19:28:00 2025 -0400
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Sat May 24 19:28:00 2025 -0400

    Bug 1956034 - Change order of panel actions to mitigate erroneous closure of unrelated panels. r=edicharry


    When the user clicks outside an open action panel, it automatically
    closes. The `popuphidden` event will cause the panel to be removed from
    the DOM. For unknown reasons, this removal from the DOM right after it
    has been hidden, causes the (unrelated) permission panel to be closed as
    well. This can be mitigated if the removal is deferred by a timeout.
    After working with the code, I decided to fix it differently:

    1. Remove the inherited special handling from Firefox for this panel.
    They keep it as a pre-load panel and swap browsers in and out. We just
    use it as a normal panel.

    2. Keep the panel in the DOM and only remove the browser when it was
    closed.

    3. When a new panel is opened, the old one is removed first (this fixes
    the bug)

    While writing the test, I run into another bug: The code in
    `ExtensionsUI.sys.mjs` breaks if there is no browser in the current
    mail3pane window. The test is not setting up an account and runs with an
    empty mail3pane window. The bug can also be reproduced in a normal
    profile by defining an empty homepage and not selecting any message.

    Since Thunderbird is not actually storing notifications per tab/browser,
    but per window, this bug is fixed by also storing `pendingNotifications`
    per window, and either pull the window from `browser.ownerGlobal` or
    from the most recent mail3pane window directly. The `browser` will be
    `null` in this case, but that does not matter. It is not actually
    used.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D250536

